E["npc:bloodmage-drazial"] = {t="npc",n="Bloodmage Drazial",z="blastedlands",s="Bloodmage Drazial is a blood elf practitioner of arcane and blood magic camped in the northern reaches of the Blasted Lands. Alongside his sister Lynnore, he studies the native beasts of the red wastes to craft potent alchemical concoctions for traveling adventurers.",h="Bloodmage Drazial is a blood elf practitioner of arcane and blood magic camped in the northern reaches of the...",sec={{t="Alchemical Studies in the Red Wastes",b="Perched near the northern pass where the Swamp of Sorrows gives way to the Blasted Lands, Bloodmage Drazial pursues a peculiar brand of magic. While many high elves shun the forbidden arts or despair over Quel'Thalas, Drazial and his sister Lynnore harness blood magic to harvest power from the harsh environment. The blighted fauna of the wastes—scorpoks, snickerfangs, and blasted boars—absorb unusual magical energies through their diet and survival in the crimson soil. By harvesting specific organs and tissues from these creatures, Drazial brews volatile concoctions that grant immense bursts of physical strength, agility, and endurance.",sp=0},{t="An Independent Supplier",b="Unlike many factional agents stationed in the Blasted Lands, Drazial operates with practical detachment. He holds no official allegiance to either the Alliance or the Horde, choosing instead to trade his alchemical expertise to anyone hardy enough to brave the wasteland and gather the raw ingredients he requires. As long as travelers bring him the organs of the local predators, Drazial is content to keep his cauldrons bubbling.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Bloodmage Drazial?",a="Bloodmage Drazial is a blood elf mage stationed near the northern entrance of the Blasted Lands. Together with his sister Lynnore, he studies the local wildlife and brews powerful alchemical reagents using parts collected from the area's corrupted beasts.",al={"who is drazial","drazial lore","bloodmage drazial npc"}},{q="Why is Drazial collecting animal parts?",a="The creatures of the Blasted Lands have adapted to survive on blighted, magically charged terrain. Drazial uses the potent internal organs of boars, hyenas, scorpions, and basilisks to concoct specialized elixirs that bolster a warrior's physical prowess.",al={"why does drazial want boar lungs","drazial quest items","drazial animal organs"}},{q="Does Drazial work for the Alliance or the Horde?",a="Drazial is neutral toward both factions. He and Lynnore do not concern themselves with the war between Stormwind and the Horde, readily dealing with any adventurer willing to supply their magical and alchemical research.",al={"drazial faction","is drazial horde or alliance","can alliance talk to drazial"}},{q="Who is the other blood elf camped with him?",a="The elf beside him is his sister, Bloodmage Lynnore. Together, the siblings practice blood magic and brew distinct concoctions from the various beasts roaming the Blasted Lands.",al={"drazial companion","who is with drazial","lynnore"}}},ang={["class:Mage"]="Drazial represents the controversial divergence of the blood elves, openly utilizing blood magic and biological reagents to synthesize arcane enhancements rather than relying strictly on traditional Kirin Tor spellcraft."},kw={"blasted boar","blasted lands","bloodmage","concoctions","drazial","lynnore","scorpok","snickerfang"},rel={"zone:blastedlands","topic:alliance","topic:horde"},src={"Bloodmage Drazial"}}
E["npc:bloodmage-lynnore"] = {t="npc",n="Bloodmage Lynnore",z="blastedlands",s="Bloodmage Lynnore is a blood elf practitioner of forbidden blood magic stationed within the Dreadmaul Furnace in the Blasted Lands. She assists Horde adventurers by concocting potent alchemical draughts from local beasts and unraveling the demonic mysteries binding the shattered demon hunter Loramus Thalipedes.",h="Bloodmage Lynnore is a blood elf practitioner of forbidden blood magic stationed within the Dreadmaul Furnace...",sec={{t="Master of Blood Magic",b="Secluded within the volcanic depths of the Dreadmaul Furnace, Bloodmage Lynnore is one of the exceptionally rare elven practitioners of blood magic found in the Eastern Kingdoms. Unperturbed by the harsh and corrupting landscape of the Blasted Lands, she studies the latent arcane and vital energies coursing through native beasts. Horde travelers who bring her the brains and gizzards of local fauna find that she can distill these gruesome reagents into specialized elixirs granting profound enhancements to intellect and spirit.",sp=0},{t="The Fate of Loramus",b="Beyond her concoctions, Lynnore plays a vital role in investigating the fell powers that plague the region. Working alongside Horde emissaries, she utilizes bloodstones and dark rituals to pierce the defenses of demonic lieutenants scattered across the wastes. She remains steadfast in the belief that the uncharted limits of blood magic can mend even the most catastrophic spiritual and physical wounds, including the dire fate that has befallen the demon hunter Loramus Thalipedes.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Bloodmage Lynnore?",a="Bloodmage Lynnore is a blood elf blood mage located in the Dreadmaul Furnace in the Blasted Lands. She serves as a quest giver and alchemical specialist aligned with the Horde, offering powerful stat-enhancing concoctions in exchange for beast parts.",al={"who is lynnore","bloodmage lynnore lore","lynnore blasted lands"}},{q="Where can Bloodmage Lynnore be found?",a="She makes her camp inside the Dreadmaul Furnace, a cave network inhabited by ogres nestled in the northern mountains of the Blasted Lands.",al={"lynnore location","where is lynnore","how to find bloodmage lynnore"}},{q="What concoctions does she brew?",a="Lynnore uses parts scavenged from the local wildlife—such as basilisk brains, vulture gizzards, and snickerfang jowls—to brew rare tonics like the Cerebral Cortex Compound and Gizzard Gum, which grant prolonged enhancements to intellect and spirit.",al={"lynnore buffs","blasted lands consumables","cerebral cortex compound"}},{q="What is her connection to Loramus Thalipedes?",a="Lynnore works to assist the demon hunter Loramus Thalipedes in his crusade against the dreadlords of the Blasted Lands. She believes that the frontiers of blood magic hold the key to sustaining him and rectifying whatever dark misfortune has struck him.",al={"lynnore loramus","loramus thalipedes bloodmage","why does lynnore care about loramus"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Lynnore acts as a valuable tactical contact in the Blasted Lands, trading unique alchemical reagents and offering dark arcane expertise to advance Horde power against local demonic threats.",["class:Mage"]="For mages fascinated by unconventional spellcraft, Lynnore represents an elusive and controversial branch of arcane philosophy that manipulates vital essence rather than conventional ley energies."},kw={"blasted lands","blood magic","bloodmage lynnore","cerebral cortex compound","dreadmaul furnace","gizzard gum","loramus thalipedes","lynnore"},rel={"subzone:dreadmaul-furnace","zone:blastedlands","npc:loramus-thalipedes","topic:horde"},src={"Bloodmage Lynnore"}}
E["npc:daio-the-decrepit"] = {t="npc",n="Daio the Decrepit",z="blastedlands",s="Daio the Decrepit is an elderly human warlock dwelling on an isolated cliffside overlooking the Tainted Scar in the Blasted Lands. Formerly an arcane scholar of Dalaran, he abandoned the Kirin Tor to dedicate his life to understanding, summoning, and suppressing demons.",h="Daio the Decrepit is an elderly human warlock dwelling on an isolated cliffside overlooking the Tainted Scar...",sec={{t="A Life in the Shadows of Dalaran",b="Long before taking up his solitary roost above the demon-infested red wastes, Daio was a mage of the Kirin Tor. His life changed forever when he assisted an ambitious conjurer named Arrexis in a catastrophic ritual. The spell went horrifically wrong, summoning an eredar mage-hunter that slaughtered Arrexis and his entire assembly of arcane apprentices. Following the massacre and his subsequent exile from the Violet Citadel, Daio turned away from pure arcane magic. Believing that ignorance of the Nether was the Kirin Tor's greatest flaw, he devoted his remaining years to studying fel magic, binding demonic entities, and understanding the precise sacrifices demanded by such terrible power.",sp=0},{t="Master of Demonic Suppression",b="Perched precariously in the northern reaches of the Tainted Scar, Daio spends his days experimenting with the dark forces that saturate the Blasted Lands. Seasoned warlocks who seek out his altar learn that mastery over the Nether requires rigid discipline, intricate containment vessels, and absolute mental fortitude. Daio insists that raw power means nothing without the will to suppress and enslave what has been called forth, reminding pupils that wielding fel energy always demands a grave and inevitable cost.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Daio the Decrepit?",a="Daio is an exiled human mage of Dalaran who renounced the arcane to study demonic magic. He now lives as an hermit warlock on the cliffs overlooking the Tainted Scar.",al={"who is daio","daio backstory","daio lore"}},{q="Why was Daio exiled from Dalaran?",a="He assisted a mage named Arrexis with a reckless conjuration ritual. The spell breached the Nether and summoned a lethal demon that slaughtered Arrexis and his followers, leading to Daio's permanent banishment.",al={"why was daio kicked out of kirin tor","daio arrexis ritual"}},{q="What is he doing in the Blasted Lands?",a="Daio studies fel energy and demonology in the shadow of the Dark Portal, using the proximity of the Burning Legion forces in the Tainted Scar to experiment with binding rituals and demonic containment.",al={"why is daio in blasted lands","daio location"}},{q="Why do warlocks seek him out?",a="Advanced practitioners travel to his altar to study the arts of demonic suppression and confinement, learning how to prepare the necessary prisons and wards required to enslave potent greater demons.",al={"warlock quest daio","what does daio teach"}}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="Daio serves as an invaluable, cynical mentor for practitioners seeking to master the dangerous art of subjugating greater demons through containment rituals.",["class:Mage"]="Daio represents a grim cautionary tale of what happens when Kirin Tor conjuration experiments spin out of control and arcane scholars fall into fel obsession."},kw={"arrexis","blasted lands","daio","daio the decrepit","demonology","kirin tor","suppression","tainted scar"},rel={"subzone:tainted-scar","zone:blastedlands"},src={"Daio the Decrepit"}}
E["npc:thadius-grimshade"] = {t="npc",n="Thadius Grimshade",z="blastedlands",s="Thadius Grimshade is a Wildhammer dwarf diviner dwelling within the mage tower of Nethergarde Keep in the Blasted Lands. Though he parted ways with Aerie Peak long ago to study esoteric and darker magical arts, he remains loyal to his kin at heart.",h="Thadius Grimshade is a Wildhammer dwarf diviner dwelling within the mage tower of Nethergarde Keep in the...",sec={{t="A Wildhammer in the Wastes",b="Unlike most Wildhammer dwarves who prefer the open skies and roaring winds of the Hinterlands, Thadius Grimshade makes his home inside Nethergarde Keep. Driven by a thirst for arcane divination and darker mystic lore, he relocated to the edge of the tainted Blasted Lands to pursue his esoteric studies. Despite his brooding discipline and separation from his clan, he retains a deep fondness for his homeland and gryphonkind, offering his rare scrying talents to those who come seeking aid on behalf of Aerie Peak.",sp=0},{t="The Price of Divination",b="When Gryphon Master Talonaxe seeks to locate the captured gryphon Sharpbeak, Thadius is called upon to perform a divination ritual using one of the beast's feathers. His magical insight does not come without a price: Thadius demands the medallion worn by the troll necromancer Nekrum Gutchewer. Seeking to unlock its secret of unnatural longevity while evading its harmful corruptions, he takes the artifact in exchange for piercing the veil of Jintha'Alor and revealing where Sharpbeak is held.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Thadius Grimshade?",a="He is an eccentric Wildhammer dwarf mage and diviner stationed in Nethergarde Keep. He left his mountain home to pursue darker, unorthodox magical arts far to the south.",al={"thadius grimshade","who is thadius","thadius npc"}},{q="Where can Thadius Grimshade be found?",a="He resides inside the high wizard tower of Nethergarde Keep, an Alliance stronghold situated in the northern reaches of the Blasted Lands.",al={"thadius location","where is thadius grimshade","thadius blasted lands"}},{q="Why does he want Nekrum's Medallion?",a="Thadius wishes to study the medallion carried by Nekrum Gutchewer to decipher how its magical power grants long life, hoping to claim that longevity without succumbing to its sinister side effects.",al={"nekrums medallion thadius","why thadius wants medallion","nekrum gutchewer medallion"}},{q="How does he help find Sharpbeak?",a="Using a feather shed by the lost gryphon and the power fueled by Nekrum's Medallion, Thadius conducts a scrying ritual that reveals Sharpbeak is imprisoned at the heights of Jintha'Alor in the Hinterlands.",al={"thadius sharpbeak","divining sharpbeak","finding sharpbeak quest"},sp=1}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="Fellow dwarves will find Thadius an oddity among Wildhammers; rather than soaring on gryphons, he spends his years buried in arcane study within a human fortress.",["class:Mage"]="Mages visiting Nethergarde will recognize Thadius as a practitioner of rare and esoteric divination methods, willing to examine troll relics to master longevity magic."},kw={"blasted lands","diviner","nekrum gutchewer","nethergarde keep","sharpbeak","thadius grimshade","wildhammer"},rel={"subzone:nethergarde-keep","zone:blastedlands","zone:hinterlands","topic:dwarf"},src={"Thadius Grimshade"}}
E["subzone:bloodwash-cavern"] = {t="subzone",n="Bloodwash Cavern",z="blastedlands",s="Bloodwash Cavern is a sprawling coastal cave located along the Red Reaches in the southeastern Blasted Lands. The cavern serves as a stronghold for the Bloodwash naga, who have occupied its ancient elven ruins and enslaved the local murloc population.",h="Bloodwash Cavern is a sprawling coastal cave located along the Red Reaches in the southeastern Blasted Lands.",sec={{t="A Serpent Stronghold",b="Tucked away along the coastline beneath the Red Reaches, Bloodwash Cavern provides a sheltered haven from the arid, corrupted wastes above. Within the cavern's damp recesses lie ancient elven stone ruins, hints of an era long predating the sundering of the world. The Bloodwash naga have taken deep root among these submerged structures, turning the cavern into a fortified redoubt where they force subjugated murloc thralls to toil under their watchful command.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Bloodwash Cavern?",a="Bloodwash Cavern is a large seaside cave along the shores of the Red Reaches in the Blasted Lands. It is controlled by the Bloodwash naga, who use it as a fortified base amidst submerged ancient elven ruins.",al={"bloodwash cave","naga cave blasted lands","what is this cave"}},{q="Why are there naga in the Blasted Lands?",a="The Bloodwash naga have established a presence along the coast of the Red Reaches and inside Bloodwash Cavern. From these coastal waters, they exploit ancient submerged elven architecture and enforce dominance over the local shoreline.",al={"why are naga here","bloodwash naga"}},{q="Why are there murlocs inside the cavern?",a="The local Rockpool murlocs have been dominated and subjugated by the Bloodwash naga. The naga force them into servitude within the cavern, working them as expendable laborers under the lash.",al={"murloc slaves","enslaved murlocs"}},{q="Why are there elven ruins inside the cave?",a="Before the Great Sundering, highborne civilization stretched across much of ancient Kalimdor. These stone structures are ancient remnants preserved underground along the coastline, drawing the naga back to echoes of their forgotten past.",al={"elf ruins blasted lands cave","ancient ruins"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="The sunken architecture within Bloodwash Cavern serves as a grim reminder of ancient Kaldorei civilization, now defiled and inhabited by their twisted, cursed naga kin."},kw={"blasted lands","bloodwash cavern","bloodwash naga","murloc","red reaches","rockpool"},rel={"subzone:red-reaches","zone:blastedlands","topic:naga","topic:murloc"},src={"Bloodwash Cavern"}}
E["subzone:dark-portal"] = {t="subzone",n="Dark Portal",z="blastedlands",s="The Dark Portal is a monumental stone gateway standing at the southern rim of the Blasted Lands. First torn open through the combined sorcery of Medivh and Gul'dan, it served as the fateful conduit that brought the Old Horde into Azeroth, initiating the First War.",h="The Dark Portal is a monumental stone gateway standing at the southern rim of the Blasted Lands.",sec={{t="A Rift Across Realities",b="Before its opening, this region was part of the Black Morass, a sodden wetland that stretched across the south. That changed when Medivh, possessed by Sargeras, joined his Tirisfal magics with the fel sorcery of Gul'dan on Draenor. The ritual drained untold lives and tore the fabric of reality apart. The Old Horde raised massive stone architecture to anchor the rift, marching armies through its threshold to shatter the Kingdom of Stormwind in the First War. The portal's fel emanations fundamentally corrupted the surrounding terrain, reducing lush marshes to the red, petrified wastes seen today.",sp=0},{t="Dormant Vigilance",b="Following the Alliance of Lordaeron's victory in the Second War, Archmage Khadgar shattered the physical stone frame with powerful magics, hoping to sever Draenor forever. However, the dimensional tear beneath proved functionally indestructible. The Alliance erected Nethergarde Keep nearby to watch the scar, while demons and remnants of the Shadow Council continue to slink through the blasted caldera. Today the gateway stands reassembled yet dormant, a silent scar between worlds that neither side dares abandon.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Can you walk through the Dark Portal right now?",a="No. The gateway's stone frame stands intact, but the rift within is dormant. No traveler can cross the threshold at this time.",al={"can i enter the dark portal","is dark portal open","portal to outland"}},{q="Who originally built the Dark Portal?",a="It was created through a joint ritual between the human Guardian Medivh on Azeroth and the warlock Gul'dan on the dying world of Draenor, orchestrating the invasion that ignited the First War.",al={"who created dark portal","medivh guldan portal","dark portal creators"}},{q="Why does Nethergarde Keep watch over it?",a="After Archmage Khadgar shattered the portal's initial frame after the Second War, he realized the dimensional rift lingered invisibly. Nethergarde Keep was founded by the Alliance to maintain a permanent watch over the site in case threats emerged again.",al={"why is nethergarde keep here","nethergarde portal watch","why nethergarde"}},{q="Why is the ground around the portal red and barren?",a="The Blasted Lands were once a fertile swamp known as the Black Morass. The vast fel energies required to breach reality, coupled with the corruption flowing from Draenor and demonic beasts, poisoned the soil and petrified the ecosystem.",al={"why are blasted lands dead","portal corruption","why is blasted lands red"}}},ang={["race:Orc"]="The portal is the painful threshold of your people's past—the gate through which the Old Horde marched in thrall to demonic masters, abandoning their ancestral homeland for war.",["faction:Alliance"]="For the Alliance, the portal is a solemn monument to the First War and the fall of ancient Stormwind, necessitating the perpetual vigil held by the mages of Nethergarde."},kw={"black morass","blasted lands","dark portal","draenor","great portal","guldan","khadgar","medivh"},rel={"zone:blastedlands","subzone:nethergarde-keep","topic:medivh","topic:old-horde","topic:first-war","topic:second-war","topic:burning-legion","topic:alliance-of-lordaeron"},src={"Dark Portal"}}
E["subzone:dreadmaul-furnace"] = {t="subzone",n="Dreadmaul Furnace",z="blastedlands",s="The Dreadmaul Furnace is a smoldering volcanic hollow within the Blasted Lands, situated just northwest of Dreadmaul Post. Carved into the rugged terrain occupied by the Dreadmaul ogres, it serves as a perilous haven where unusual truces have been struck in the shadow of dark sorcery.",h="The Dreadmaul Furnace is a smoldering volcanic hollow within the Blasted Lands, situated just northwest of...",sec={{t="A Precarious Pact",b="Tucked into the craggy hills northwest of Dreadmaul Post, the Dreadmaul Furnace is primarily the domain of the local Dreadmaul ogres. Despite the violent nature of these brutish creatures, an uneasy arrangement allows the elven siblings Lynnore and Drazial to dwell within a carved-out chamber of the mound. Operating in such close proximity to volatile ogre sorcery and the harsh wastes of the Blasted Lands makes this furnace one of the most perilous outposts in the south.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the Dreadmaul Furnace located?",a="The Dreadmaul Furnace is nestled in the northern mountains of the Blasted Lands, directly northwest of Dreadmaul Post along the rugged border of the ogre encampment.",al={"dreadmaul furnace location","where is dreadmaul furnace","how to find dreadmaul furnace"}},{q="Who lives in the Dreadmaul Furnace?",a="The cavernous area is controlled by the Dreadmaul ogre clan, but an inner chamber houses the blood elven siblings Lynnore and Drazial, who managed to strike a delicate truce with the ogres to conduct their arcane studies in safety.",al={"who is at dreadmaul furnace","dreadmaul furnace npcs","who lives here"}},{q="Why are elves living alongside ogres?",a="Lynnore and Drazial negotiated an arrangement with the Dreadmaul clan that permits them access to the hollow. The siblings study the tainted magical properties of the Blasted Lands and the powerful artifacts left behind, remaining unmolested so long as their pact holds.",al={"why are there elves here","lynnore drazial ogres","elf ogre alliance"}}},ang={["class:Mage"]="The existence of elven scholars dwelling unmolested among brutal ogres illustrates the sheer lengths arcanists will go to study the potent magical anomalies created by the opening of the Dark Portal.",["faction:Horde"]="Positioned just above the Horde encampment at Dreadmaul Post, the Furnace is a reminder that not all negotiations in these harsh badlands run through Orgrimmar's diplomacy."},kw={"blasted lands","drazial","dreadmaul furnace","dreadmaul ogres","dreadmaul post","lynnore"},rel={"subzone:dreadmaul-post","zone:blastedlands","topic:horde"},src={"Dreadmaul Furnace"}}
E["subzone:dreadmaul-post"] = {t="subzone",n="Dreadmaul Post",z="blastedlands",s="Dreadmaul Post is an entrenched ogre settlement situated in the scorched wastes of the Blasted Lands. Established by the Dreadmaul clan, this mound serves as a fortified redoubt near the Dark Portal where ogres have lingered since their arrival from Draenor. Travelers passing through the region must contend with these fierce brutes and the treacherous terrain surrounding their encampment.",h="Dreadmaul Post is an entrenched ogre settlement situated in the scorched wastes of the Blasted Lands.",sec={{t="Remnants of Draenor",b="When the Horde surged through the Dark Portal in decades past, clans of ogres marched alongside them into Azeroth. The Dreadmaul clan chose to dig in near the gateway itself, raising crude stone mounds and earthworks across the red wastes of the Blasted Lands. Dreadmaul Post stands as one of their primary outposts, maintaining a firm grip over the badlands and clashing with wandering beasts, lost draenei survivors, and any travelers foolish enough to draw near their territory.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who lives at Dreadmaul Post?",a="Dreadmaul Post is inhabited by the Dreadmaul clan of ogres. These hulking brutes crossed over from Draenor through the Dark Portal during the wars and established a permanent foothold in the desolate crags of the Blasted Lands.",al={"who is at dreadmaul post","dreadmaul post inhabitants","dreadmaul ogres"}},{q="Why are the ogres still in the Blasted Lands?",a="Following the Old Horde's collapse and the sealing of the Dark Portal, many ogres scattered across Azeroth. The Dreadmaul clan, however, stayed close to their original entry point, making the scarred, desolate expanse around the dormant rift their home.",al={"why dreadmaul here","ogres blasted lands","why ogres near portal"}},{q="Who else wanders the area near the post?",a="Aside from fierce local predators like scorpid and basilisks, occasional sorrowful, displaced draenei survivors wander the red desert near Dreadmaul Post, stranded far from their shattered homeworld.",al={"draenei blasted lands","who is near dreadmaul","creatures dreadmaul post"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Although ogres once fought alongside the Old Horde, wild clans like the Dreadmaul have long severed ties with Thrall's new order, viewing all travelers as hostile invaders.",["faction:Alliance"]="For Alliance scouts monitoring the Dark Portal, the Dreadmaul ogres represent an entrenched, violent hazard that complicates any patrol through the southern reaches of the continent."},kw={"blasted lands","dark portal","dreadmaul","dreadmaul post","ogre mound","ogres"},rel={"zone:blastedlands","subzone:dark-portal","subzone:maul-subzone"},src={"Dreadmaul Post"}}
E["subzone:forge-grounds"] = {t="subzone",n="Forge Grounds",z="blastedlands",s="In the arid reaches of the Blasted Lands, the area outside the Nethergarde Mines functions as an Alliance logistical and support hub known as the Nethergarde Supply Camps. In the current era of 25 ADP, it remains under the stewardship of Nethergarde Keep to support ongoing excavation work.",h="In the arid reaches of the Blasted Lands, the area outside the Nethergarde Mines functions as an Alliance...",sec={{t="Outpost of the Keep",b="Situated just outside the entrances of the Nethergarde Mines, this camp provides essential provisions, tools, and security for the miners working deep beneath the red hills of the Blasted Lands. Run under the authority of Nethergarde Keep, the staging area ensures a steady flow of materials needed to reinforce Alliance watchposts monitoring the Dark Portal. For travelers heading along the jagged ridges, the camp stands as one of the few signs of organized industry amid the blighted wilderness.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of this camp?",a="The encampment exists to support the excavators and laborers operating within the nearby Nethergarde Mines. It provides a staging area for equipment, storage, and supplies necessary to sustain operations in the hostile environment of the Blasted Lands.",al={"why is this camp here","forge grounds purpose","supply camp blasted lands"}},{q="Who controls this area?",a="The grounds are maintained by the Alliance garrison based out of Nethergarde Keep, ensuring mining efforts proceed without disruption from local predators and hostile forces.",al={"who owns forge grounds","who runs the supply camp","alliance or horde"}},{q="Why is it sometimes referred to as the Forge Grounds?",a="While known in 25 ADP primarily as part of the Nethergarde supply infrastructure, the presence of metalworking tools, anvils, and mining logistics often leads travelers to refer to the staging area around the mine entrance by its forging works.",al={"why forge grounds","forge grounds name"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="The supply grounds secure critical material pipelines that keep Nethergarde Keep supplied against potential threats emerging from the Dark Portal.",["profession:Mining"]="Miners working nearby rely on this outpost as a staging ground before venturing into the mineral-rich tunnels beneath the Blasted Lands."},kw={"alliance","blasted lands","forge grounds","nethergarde","nethergarde mines","nethergarde supply camps"},rel={"subzone:nethergarde-supply-camps","subzone:nethergarde-mines","zone:blastedlands"},src={"Forge Grounds"}}
E["subzone:garrison-armory"] = {t="subzone",n="Garrison Armory",z="blastedlands",s="The Garrison Armory is an Alliance mining operation carved into the hills southwest of Nethergarde Keep in the Blasted Lands. Miners and engineers work the underground veins to harvest valuable minerals, sustaining the lonely fortress and shipping raw wealth back to Stormwind. It forms a crucial industrial lifeline in an otherwise blasted, barren wilderness.",h="The Garrison Armory is an Alliance mining operation carved into the hills southwest of Nethergarde Keep in...",sec={{t="A Lifeline in the Red Wastes",b="Maintaining a permanent military garrison in the arid wastes of the Blasted Lands requires constant supply, and Nethergarde Keep cannot rely purely on long supply trains from Stormwind. The Garrison Armory serves as the keep's primary industrial excavation. Nethergarde miners, overseen by foremen and assisted by engineers, work these subterranean shafts to pull valuable minerals from the earth. The ore extracted here is utilized directly by Nethergarde's smiths and fortifications or hauled back to the capital in exchange for the foodstuffs, tools, and provisions the fortress needs to maintain its vigil over the Dark Portal.",sp=0},{t="Vulnerable Industry",b="Because the armory sits away from the main walls of Nethergarde Keep, the excavation remains exposed to the harsh perils of the red desert. Trolls, ogres, and wild beasts prowl the surrounding crags, while agents of the Horde keep a close eye on Nethergarde's mining output. The workforce within the tunnels operates under armed guard, knowing that any disruption to the armory directly threatens Nethergarde's ability to maintain its watch over the blasted frontier.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Garrison Armory used for?",a="The Garrison Armory is an Alliance mining complex operated by Nethergarde Keep. Workers extract metal and minerals underground to maintain the fortress and trade back to Stormwind for essential food and equipment.",al={"garrison armory purpose","what is this mine","why is there a mine here"}},{q="Who works in the armory?",a="The mine is staffed by Nethergarde miners, engineers, and foremen affiliated with the Alliance. They work to excavate ore deposits and maintain the shafts beneath the supervision of Nethergarde's command.",al={"who is inside","armory npcs","garrison miners"}},{q="Why does Nethergarde Keep need this mine?",a="Nethergarde Keep sits isolated in the desolate Blasted Lands, making regular supply lines difficult. By extracting its own metals, the fortress can repair gear, reinforce defenses, and trade excess raw materials to Stormwind in exchange for vital survival supplies.",al={"why nethergarde needs it","armory importance","nethergarde resources"}},{q="Can Horde players enter the Garrison Armory?",a="The armory is occupied by hostile Alliance workers and guards, but Horde adventurers frequently brave the depths to claim the rich ore veins buried within the mine shafts.",al={"can horde go here","horde in garrison armory","is it safe for horde"}}},ang={["profession:Mining"]="The shafts of the Garrison Armory hold valuable mineral veins carved out of the rugged Blasted Lands stone, making it a contested subterranean quarry.",["faction:Alliance"]="The Armory's workforce labors constantly to ensure Nethergarde Keep remains supplied with weapons, armor, and trade goods to hold its lonely watch."},kw={"blasted lands","garrison armory","mine","nethergarde","nethergarde engineer","nethergarde keep","nethergarde miner","stormwind"},rel={"subzone:nethergarde-keep","zone:blastedlands","topic:stormwind-kingdom","topic:alliance","topic:horde"},src={"Garrison Armory"}}
E["subzone:maldraz"] = {t="subzone",n="Maldraz",z="blastedlands",s="Maldraz is a massive great tree situated within the Blasted Lands. Rooted amidst an otherwise scarred and demon-blighted wasteland, the colossal bough stands as a poignant reminder of nature's perilous struggle against dark corruption.",h="Maldraz is a massive great tree situated within the Blasted Lands.",sec={{t="A Beacon in the Blight",b="Rising in the southern reaches of the Blasted Lands near the tainted wastes, Maldraz is an immense tree cultivated to channel druidic energies into an environment devastated by demonic magic. While much of the Blasted Lands lies stripped of natural life following the opening of the Dark Portal, Maldraz represents a desperate effort to plant living roots deep within the corrupted soil and draw pure essence back into the shattered landscape.",sp=0},{t="The Creeping Taint",b="Nurturing verdant life in soil soaked with nether energies is fraught with profound peril. The ambient demonic residue clinging to the surrounding earth seeps relentlessly into living bark and foliage. Travelers who draw near Maldraz witness a constant tension: the noble yearning of living wood battling the insidious corruption that permeates the region's blackened earth.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Maldraz?",a="Maldraz is a colossal great tree located in the Blasted Lands. It serves as a focal point of living nature and verdant growth in a region overwhelmingly scarred by demonic contamination.",al={"what is this tree","maldraz tree","who is maldraz"}},{q="Why is there a giant tree in the Blasted Lands?",a="The tree was seeded and nurtured as an attempt to introduce resilient botanical life into the blighted expanse, defying the barren desolation left behind by dark portal energies.",al={"tree in blasted lands","why is maldraz here","green tree blasted lands"}},{q="Is Maldraz safe to visit?",a="The surrounding landscape remains dangerous and unpredictable. While the tree itself represents natural life, the pervasive demonic aura of the Blasted Lands continuously threatens any untended wilderness in the zone.",al={"is maldraz hostile","maldraz danger"}},{q="Can nature really survive in the Blasted Lands?",a="The soil of the Blasted Lands is severely drained and corrupted by fel energies, making standard plant life almost impossible to sustain. Sites like Maldraz demonstrate that powerful nature magic can take root, though holding back the persistent corruption is an unending struggle.",al={"can plants grow here","healing the blasted lands"}}},ang={["class:Druid"]="Seeing a great tree standing against the demonic taint of the Blasted Lands is both an inspiring testament to nature's tenacity and a stark warning of how easily living roots can become poisoned."},kw={"blasted lands","corruption","great tree","maldraz","nature","tainted forest","tainted scar"},rel={"zone:blastedlands","subzone:tainted-scar","topic:druid","topic:cenarion-circle"},src={"Maldraz"}}
E["subzone:nethergarde-keep"] = {t="subzone",n="Nethergarde Keep",z="blastedlands",s="Nethergarde Keep is a fortified Alliance stronghold perched high upon the bluffs along the road entering the Blasted Lands. Erected by the Stonemasons Guild after the Second War, it stands as a vigilant sentinel over the dormant Dark Portal and the chaotic energies bleeding across the red wastes. Today, mages and garrisons supported by Stormwind continue their lonely vigil against demons and lingering corruption.",h="Nethergarde Keep is a fortified Alliance stronghold perched high upon the bluffs along the road entering the...",sec={{t="A Sentinel Against the Red World",b="Following the destruction of the Dark Portal at the end of the Second War, Archmage Khadgar and the leaders of the Alliance of Lordaeron recognized that Azeroth could never again leave the rift unguarded. Under the supervision of Edwin VanCleef, the Stonemasons Guild labored to raise towering bastions, barracks, and mage spires along the canyon pass into the Blasted Lands. Staffed by Kirin Tor sorcerers, its dual purpose was to keep constant watch on the shattered gateway and weave wards preventing the demonic blight of the scorched landscape from creeping northward into the human kingdoms.",sp=0},{t="The Lonely Vigil",b="When the Dark Portal reopened and the Alliance Expedition ventured into Draenor, Khadgar and his companions sealed the gateway behind them, leaving Nethergarde to guard a silent remnant. For two decades, scholars from Dalaran and the Wizard's Sanctum have analyzed the portal's lingering energies, mutated local fauna, and demonic incursions. With Dalaran ravaged during the Third War, Nethergarde relies entirely on vital supply caravans from Stormwind City to sustain its soldiers and mages as they stand alone against the horrors haunting the wasteland.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why was Nethergarde Keep built?",a="It was commissioned after the Second War by Archmage Khadgar and the Alliance of Lordaeron to guard against another orcish invasion from Draenor and contain the spreading demonic corruption of the Blasted Lands.",al={"purpose of nethergarde","why is nethergarde here","nethergarde history"}},{q="Who constructed the keep?",a="Nethergarde Keep was built by the Stonemasons Guild under the architectural direction of Edwin VanCleef, funded jointly by the member kingdoms of the Alliance of Lordaeron.",al={"who built nethergarde","nethergarde builders","vancleef nethergarde"}},{q="Who commands and supplies the fortress now?",a="Originally maintained by Dalaran's Kirin Tor, the fortress now relies primarily on the Kingdom of Stormwind for troops, regular supply caravans, and logistical support following Dalaran's fall to the Scourge and the Legion.",al={"who runs nethergarde","nethergarde supplies","stormwind nethergarde"}},{q="What are the mages inside the keep studying?",a="Researchers from the Wizard's Sanctum study the dormant energies of the Dark Portal, the strange mutations afflicting local wildlife, and methods to ward off the fel taint lingering over the red landscape.",al={"nethergarde mages","wizards sanctum nethergarde","what are they researching"}}},ang={["class:Mage"]="For practitioners of the arcane, Nethergarde represents decades of Kirin Tor research into dimensional rifts, rift sealing, and holding back the entropic spread of fel corruption.",["faction:Alliance"]="The fortress stands as one of the Alliance's most vital forward bulwarks, paid for in blood and gold to ensure the horrors of the First and Second Wars never spill out of the portal again."},kw={"blasted lands","dark portal","keep","khadgar","kirin tor","nethergarde","stonemasons","stormwind","vancleef"},rel={"subzone:dark-portal","zone:blastedlands","topic:stonemasons-guild","zone:stormwind","topic:second-war","topic:alliance-of-lordaeron","zone:swampofsorrows"},src={"Nethergarde Keep"}}
E["subzone:nethergarde-mines"] = {t="subzone",n="Nethergarde Mines",z="blastedlands",s="Tucked into the northern hills of the Blasted Lands, the Nethergarde Mines supply vital iron and stone to nearby Nethergarde Keep. Dug deep beneath the blasted earth, these winding tunnels face mounting danger from hidden Horde infiltrators and ancient evils unearthed in the dark.",h="Tucked into the northern hills of the Blasted Lands, the Nethergarde Mines supply vital iron and stone to...",sec={{t="A Vital Lifeline",b="Carved into the jagged northern ridges of the Blasted Lands, the Nethergarde Mines are an essential resource hub for Nethergarde Keep. Overseen by Chief Prospector Hondo from his elevated office, Alliance miners work relentlessly along the cart tracks to pull usable iron from the desolate earth. Maintaining this supply line is crucial for sustaining the fortress, which watches over the blighted basin and the dormant Dark Portal. However, keeping the operation safe has proven nearly impossible.",sp=0},{t="Blood and Shadows",b="Recently, the quiet labor of the quarry turned into a battleground. Fallen defenders litter the entrance after Horde operatives covertly breached the tunnels to cut off Nethergarde's vital supply line. Worse still, deep excavations accidentally broke into a forgotten subterranean chamber, freeing an ancient demon named Illycor. Now, ordinary miners find themselves trapped between enemy infiltrators sneaking through the side passages and a waking terror lurking in the deepest shafts.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of the Nethergarde Mines?",a="The mines supply Nethergarde Keep with necessary iron, stone, and raw building materials. Because the Blasted Lands are barren and isolated, the fortress relies on these nearby excavations to reinforce its defenses and maintain its garrison.",al={"why do nethergarde mines exist","what are they digging here","nethergarde mine purpose"}},{q="Who is currently running the mining operation?",a="Chief Prospector Hondo directs the operation on behalf of Nethergarde Keep. He manages the excavation crews and oversees output from his office stationed in an upper chamber above the main cart tracks.",al={"who runs nethergarde mines","who is in charge","nethergarde mine leader"}},{q="Why is the entrance littered with dead Alliance defenders?",a="The Horde launched covert attacks against the site to disrupt supply lines running into Nethergarde Keep. Hidden infiltrators managed to overwhelm the outer sentries at the threshold, slipping operatives deep into the shafts along the rail lines.",al={"why are there bodies at the mine","who attacked nethergarde mines","dead miners entrance"}},{q="What demon was freed inside the mine?",a="Miners digging deep beneath the northern rock accidentally broke into a hidden vault and unleashed Illycor, a demon that had remained buried beneath the Blasted Lands for ages.",al={"nethergarde mine demon","who is illycor","demon in the mine"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="The iron extracted here keeps Nethergarde Keep armed and fortified against the hostile forces of the Blasted Lands, making the defense of these tunnels a vital priority.",["profession:Mining"]="These deep shafts tap into subterranean iron veins running beneath the otherwise scorched and lifeless terrain of the Blasted Lands."},kw={"blasted lands","hondo","illycor","infiltrators","iron","mines","nethergarde"},rel={"subzone:nethergarde-keep","zone:blastedlands","topic:alliance","topic:horde"},src={"Nethergarde Mines"}}
E["subzone:nethergarde-supply-camps"] = {t="subzone",n="Nethergarde Supply Camps",z="blastedlands",s="The Nethergarde Supply Camps sit directly outside the Nethergarde Mines in the northern reaches of the Blasted Lands. What was meant to be a secure logistical hub providing provisions and smithing facilities for the fortress has erupted into an active skirmish between Alliance defenders and attacking Horde troops.",h="The Nethergarde Supply Camps sit directly outside the Nethergarde Mines in the northern reaches of the...",sec={{t="A Frontline at the Gates",b="Positioned just outside the entrance to the Nethergarde Mines, the supply camps provide vital staging, equipment, and field repair facilities for Nethergarde Keep. Complete with working anvils and forges, the post should be an orderly depot keeping the fortress supplied. Instead, it has become a hot combat zone. The Horde, pushing forces into the Blasted Lands, has launched an assault led by Captain Metlek and his Okril'lon infantry, leaving Alliance defenders fighting desperately among the scattered crates and tents to prevent their vital logistics from falling into enemy hands.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why are the Horde and Alliance fighting here?",a="The camps contain key logistical infrastructure, stockpiled provisions, and metalworking equipment for Nethergarde Keep. Captain Metlek has led the Okril'lon vanguard to sever these supply lines and weaken the Alliance foothold in the Blasted Lands.",al={"why fighting nethergarde camps","who is attacking supply camps","why horde here"}},{q="Who leads the Horde assault on the camps?",a="Captain Metlek commands the Okril'lon infantry attacking the camps, orchestrating the push to overrun the defenders and secure the supply hub.",al={"supply camps horde leader","captain metlek","who leads okrillon here"}},{q="What amenities exist in these camps?",a="One of the encampments maintains a working forge and anvil, utilized for maintaining and repairing the weapons and gear needed by troops stationed in the harsh environment.",al={"forge in supply camps","anvil blasted lands nethergarde"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Holding these supply depots is essential for sustaining Nethergarde Keep against growing threats across the blasted red wastes.",["faction:Horde"]="Striking the supply camps cuts into Nethergarde's critical resources and asserts Horde dominance in the region."},kw={"blasted lands","captain metlek","nethergarde","nethergarde mines","nethergarde supply camps","okrillon","supply camp"},rel={"subzone:nethergarde-mines","zone:blastedlands","topic:alliance","topic:horde"},src={"Nethergarde Supply Camps"}}
E["subzone:okril-lon-hold"] = {t="subzone",n="Okril'lon Hold",z="blastedlands",s="Perched in the northwestern crags of the Blasted Lands, this fortified stronghold was originally built by the Old Horde as Rockard during the First War. In the current era of 25 ADP, it is firmly occupied by the brutal Dreadmaul ogres under the name Dreadmaul Hold. The encampment serves as a fortified redoubt overlooking the scorched red plains below.",h="Perched in the northwestern crags of the Blasted Lands, this fortified stronghold was originally built by the...",sec={{t="From Rockard to Dreadmaul Hold",b="Long before the scorched expanse of the Blasted Lands emerged from the Black Morass, orcish invaders constructed Rockard alongside Stonard as one of the first settlements established on Azeroth after the Dark Portal opened. Though it survived the devastation of both the First and Second Wars, the departing orcs could not hold it. The Dreadmaul clan of ogres stormed the fortress, driving out any remaining defenders and claiming the stone towers and blacksmith for themselves. Renamed Dreadmaul Hold, it now serves as the primary garrison of the region's ogre population.",sp=0},{t="A Den of Ogre Supremacy",b="Under the iron rule of Grol the Destroyer, Dreadmaul Hold has become a nexus of brute force and dark allegiances. Enslaved or allied to the dreadlord Razelikh the Defiler, the ogres guard key mountain paths leading north toward the Swamp of Sorrows. Travelers and Horde supply trains skirting the northern mountains must remain ever vigilant against raiding warbands surging out of its gates.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is this place called Dreadmaul Hold instead of Okril'lon Hold?",a="In 25 ADP, the stronghold is known solely as Dreadmaul Hold. It was seized by the Dreadmaul ogres following the Second War. Any claims of Horde reconquest or renaming under Warmatron Okrilla belong to later years that have not occurred.",al={"dreadmaul hold name","is this okrillon","why dreadmaul"}},{q="What was this settlement originally?",a="It was originally built as Rockard, an early outpost of the Old Horde established in the Black Morass shortly after the Dark Portal opened during the First War, making it one of the oldest orc settlements on Azeroth.",al={"who built this fortress","original name of dreadmaul hold","rockard history"}},{q="Who rules Dreadmaul Hold right now?",a="The hold is led by the ogre warlord Grol the Destroyer, who commands the Dreadmaul clan in the Blasted Lands and serves the demon Razelikh the Defiler.",al={"dreadmaul boss","who leads the ogres here","grol the destroyer"}},{q="Is the Horde in control of this base?",a="No. The fortress is entirely hostile to both the Horde and the Alliance, occupied solely by the Dreadmaul ogres.",al={"is dreadmaul horde","friendly base blasted lands"}}},ang={["race:Orc"]="Rockard was one of your people's earliest footholds on this world, and seeing it defiled and overrun by Dreadmaul ogres is a bitter reminder of the Old Horde's scattered collapse.",["faction:Alliance"]="Sitting right on the northern threshold of the Blasted Lands, the fortified hold represents a constant threat of ogre warbands ambushing patrols riding south from the Swamp of Sorrows."},kw={"black morass","blasted lands","dreadmaul hold","dreadmaul ogres","grol the destroyer","okril'lon hold","rockard"},rel={"zone:blastedlands","subzone:stonard","subzone:dark-portal","subzone:nethergarde-keep","npc:fallen-hero-of-the-horde","npc:loramus-thalipedes","topic:first-war","topic:second-war"},src={"Okril'lon Hold"}}
E["subzone:red-reaches"] = {t="subzone",n="Red Reaches",z="blastedlands",s="The Red Reaches is the harsh, sunbaked southeastern coastline of the Blasted Lands. Sheltered below the jagged red cliffs, its waters are dominated by a bitter struggle between the native Rockpool murlocs and the tyrannical Bloodwash naga.",h="The Red Reaches is the harsh, sunbaked southeastern coastline of the Blasted Lands.",sec={{t="A Shattered Peace",b="Running along the ocean border of the desolate Blasted Lands, the Red Reaches provides a sharp contrast between arid red rock and pounding ocean surf. For a time, the local Rockpool murloc tribes and the Bloodwash naga dwelled alongside one another in an uneasy coexistence, united partly by their shared veneration of Neptulon, the Tidehunter. That harmony dissolved when the naga asserted brutal supremacy over the coastline, turning on their former neighbors. The naga enslaved the Rockpool tribes, forcing captive murlocs into cruel gladiatorial combat and sacrificial rites.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where are the Red Reaches located?",a="The Red Reaches forms the southeastern shore of the Blasted Lands, tucked beneath the towering red cliffs along the Great Sea.",al={"where is red reaches","red reaches location","red reaches blasted lands"}},{q="Who inhabits the Red Reaches?",a="The coastline is inhabited primarily by the Bloodwash naga and the Rockpool murlocs, alongside coastal wildlife like crabs.",al={"who lives here","red reaches mobs","what is at red reaches"}},{q="Why are the naga and murlocs fighting here?",a="While both groups once lived side by side and shared worship of the water elemental lord Neptulon, the Bloodwash naga betrayed the murlocs, enslaving them and sacrificing them for dark ends.",al={"why naga fight murlocs","bloodwash naga rockpool murlocs","why are murlocs enslaved"}},{q="Is there any connection between this beach and the Dark Portal?",a="The beach sits far down on the coast away from the Dark Portal, largely isolated from the demonic forces and Nethergarde mages fighting inland.",al={"dark portal connection","red reaches dark portal"}}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="The twisted reverence the Bloodwash naga hold toward Neptulon, Lord of Tides, stands as an affront to any shaman dedicated to maintaining balance with the Elemental Lords."},kw={"blasted lands","bloodwash","murloc","naga","neptulon","red reaches","rockpool"},rel={"zone:blastedlands","topic:naga","topic:murloc"},src={"Red Reaches"}}
E["subzone:rockpool-village"] = {t="subzone",n="Rockpool Village",z="blastedlands",s="Rockpool Village is a seaside settlement nestled along the eastern coast of the Blasted Lands. Originally inhabited by the Rockpool tribe of murlocs, the village was violently seized by the hostile Bloodwash naga.",h="Rockpool Village is a seaside settlement nestled along the eastern coast of the Blasted Lands.",sec={{t="A Conquered Shore",b="Tucked away along the Red Reaches on the Blasted Lands' eastern coastline, Rockpool Village was once a quiet enclave for the Rockpool murlocs. That precarious existence ended when the Bloodwash naga surged from the ocean depths. Rather than simply driving the tribe out, the serpentine invaders captured the village outright and enslaved the remaining murloc populace. Today, the settlement stands under harsh naga control, with its former residents forced into cruel subjugation beneath the overlooking bluffs.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Rockpool Village located?",a="Rockpool Village lies along the eastern coast of the Blasted Lands, in the coastal strip known as the Red Reaches.",al={"rockpool location","where is rockpool village","blasted lands murloc camp"}},{q="Who lives in Rockpool Village now?",a="The settlement is dominated by the Bloodwash naga, who conquered the village and forced the surviving Rockpool murlocs into servitude.",al={"who is at rockpool village","rockpool enemies","who controls rockpool"}},{q="Who was Neptool?",a="Neptool was the chieftain of the Rockpool tribe. Following the conquest of his home by the naga, his ghost lingers on the roadway overlooking the village below.",al={"ghost murloc blasted lands","chief neptool","who is neptool"}},{q="Why did the naga take the village?",a="The Bloodwash naga pushed ashore along the Red Reaches to secure a foothold on the mainland, seizing the village to subjugate and enslave the native murlocs.",al={"why did naga attack rockpool","bloodwash invasion"}}},kw={"blasted lands","bloodwash","neptool","red reaches","rockpool","rockpool village"},rel={"subzone:red-reaches","zone:blastedlands","topic:murloc","topic:naga"},src={"Rockpool Village"}}
E["subzone:serpent-s-coil"] = {t="subzone",n="Serpent's Coil",z="blastedlands",s="Serpent's Coil is a winding network of caves and burnt-out encampments nestled in the eastern ridges of the Blasted Lands. Littered with scorched orcish architecture left behind from the older wars, it serves as a secluded redoubt for dark cultists and solitary researchers.",h="Serpent's Coil is a winding network of caves and burnt-out encampments nestled in the eastern ridges of the...",sec={{t="A Labyrinth of Ash and Stone",b="Carved into the jagged eastern cliffs of the Blasted Lands, the winding path and caverns of Serpent's Coil wind past ruined orcish huts that date back to the First and Second Wars. Rather than simple beasts, the tunnels harbor cabals of Shadowsworn cultists and practitioners of dark arts drawn to the residual demonic energies permeating the red wastes. Deep within its twisting hollows, odd figures pursue private obsessions far from the watchful eyes of Nethergarde Keep.",sp=0},{t="The Cultist Lair",b="The caverns have long served as a staging ground for Archmage Allistarj's cultists, who revere demonic lords and experiment with sinister artifacts like the Amulet of Allistarj. Even when their master's grasp wavers, loyal Shadowsworn zealots continue to patrol the cave turns, maintaining rituals in Kirith the Damned's service while hiding behind scorched barricades.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is Serpent's Coil?",a="Serpent's Coil is a winding cave network and canyon located in the eastern Blasted Lands, known for its charred orcish ruins and sinister occupants.",al={"serpents coil","what is this cave","blasted lands serpent coil"}},{q="Why are there old orc structures here?",a="The encampment structures date back to the First and Second Wars when the Old Horde crossed through the nearby Dark Portal and fortified the surrounding region before their defeat.",al={"why orc ruins","orc buildings blasted lands","burnt huts"}},{q="Who lives inside Serpent's Coil?",a="The caverns are occupied by Shadowsworn cultists aligned with Archmage Allistarj and dark powers, alongside isolated individuals studying the unusual magic of the Blasted Lands.",al={"who is here","serpent coil enemies","who controls the cave"}},{q="Why is there an Alliance gnome camped inside a cave surrounded by danger?",a="Kasim Sharim conducts private, dangerous magical research deep within the cavern, risking the surrounding cultists to study the potent demonic artifacts scattered throughout the territory.",al={"gnome in cave","kasim sharim","why is kasim here"}}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="The presence of a lone gnome researcher deep inside a cultist-infested cave exemplifies the fearless—or reckless—lengths gnomish intellect will go to unravel forbidden magic.",["class:Warlock"]="The Shadowsworn operating within Serpent's Coil practice binding rituals and harbor potent artifacts, making the cavern a grim reflection of reckless demonic study."},kw={"allistarj","blasted lands","kasim sharim","kirith the damned","serpent's coil","serpents coil","shadowsworn"},rel={"zone:blastedlands","topic:first-war","topic:second-war","topic:gnome","topic:horde","topic:alliance"},src={"Serpent's Coil"}}
E["subzone:shattered-beachhead"] = {t="subzone",n="Shattered Beachhead",z="blastedlands",s="The Shattered Beachhead is a coastal expanse along the jagged eastern shore of the Blasted Lands, situated north of the Shattershore. Bordered by red stone bluffs and the surging ocean, it marks an austere eastern boundary in a region scarred by dark magics.",h="The Shattered Beachhead is a coastal expanse along the jagged eastern shore of the Blasted Lands, situated...",sec={{t="A Barren Shore",b="Located along the jagged eastern coast of the Blasted Lands just north of the Shattershore, this seaside stretch is exposed to the harsh, churning waters off the eastern subcontinent. While the interior of the zone remains choked by fell sorcery and demonic corruption lingering from the opening of the Dark Portal, the shoreline here stands bare and wind-scoured against the rocks.",sp=0},{t="Coastal Geography",b="The Blasted Lands offer few hospitable approaches, and its eastern cliffs drop steeply into the surf. The Shattered Beachhead serves as one of the few low approaches where the land meets the sea, though it remains desolate and isolated from the main overland tracks traversing the red wastes.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the Shattered Beachhead located?",a="The Shattered Beachhead is situated along the far eastern coastline of the Blasted Lands, found directly north of the Shattershore bluffs.",al={"shattered beachhead location","where is shattered beachhead","how to find shattered beachhead"}},{q="What is the environment like here?",a="It is a rocky, barren coastal area marked by craggy red cliffs, rough ocean waters, and desolate shores, typical of the arid and corrupted coastline bordering the Blasted Lands.",al={"beachhead terrain","what does it look like"}},{q="Is the Shattered Beachhead inhabited?",a="In the current era of 25 ADP, the coastline remains largely deserted and wild, isolated from the major encampments and forts deeper inland.",al={"who lives here","beachhead npcs"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For Alliance scouts monitoring the perimeter of the Blasted Lands from Nethergarde Keep, the barren eastern coast remains a desolate wilderness with few natural harbors."},kw={"blasted lands","coast","shattered beachhead","shattershore","shore"},rel={"subzone:shattershore","zone:blastedlands","zone:swampofsorrows","topic:alliance"},src={"Shattered Beachhead"}}
E["subzone:shattershore"] = {t="subzone",n="Shattershore",z="blastedlands",s="Shattershore is a desolate stretch of coastline on the eastern edge of the Blasted Lands. Lined with the splintered wreckage of Gilnean vessels, its fog-swept sands are haunted by the drowned ghosts of fallen sailors and travelers.",h="Shattershore is a desolate stretch of coastline on the eastern edge of the Blasted Lands.",sec={{t="Wreckage of Gilneas",b="Stretching along the Great Sea east of the blasted red wastes, Shattershore is a maritime graveyard. The shattered hulls of ships originating from the isolationist kingdom of Gilneas lie half-buried in the surf. No living crew remains to explain how these northern vessels sailed so far south or what drove them ashore, but their drowned spirits still wander the wreckage, bound to the beach in death alongside enigmatic spectral powers like the Spirit of Grol.",sp=0},{t="The Severed Amulet",b="Hidden deep within one of the rotting cargo holds rests a gruesome artifact: the severed head of the ogre Grol, still bearing his enchanted amulet. Why Gilnean sailors transported such a dark relic across the ocean remains a mystery, but the vengeful presence of Grol's restless spirit suggests the cargo may have contributed to their doom.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is Shattershore?",a="Shattershore is the eastern coastline of the Blasted Lands bordering the Great Sea, known for its shipwrecks and spectral inhabitants.",al={"where is shattershore","shattershore location","blasted lands coast"}},{q="Why are Gilnean ships wrecked here?",a="Gilneas has long secluded itself behind the Greymane Wall, making the presence of their fleet so far south an anomaly. It is not fully known what mission drew them to the Blasted Lands or what brought down the vessels, though occult cargo and the hostile local magic are suspected.",al={"gilnean wrecks","why are gilneas ships in blasted lands","shattershore shipwrecks"}},{q="Who haunts the beach?",a="The shore is haunted by drowned Gilnean sailors, merchants, and settlers, trapped in undeath alongside ancient spirits such as the ogre Spirit of Grol.",al={"shattershore ghosts","drowned gilnean spirits","who is on shattershore"}},{q="What is hidden inside the shipwrecks?",a="Inside the hold of one ruined ship lies the preserved head of the ogre Grol, adorned with the Amulet of Grol, a talisman sought after by those studying the fell artifacts of the Blasted Lands.",al={"head of grol","amulet of grol","shattershore cargo"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Finding vessels flying Gilnean heraldry broken on the shores of the Blasted Lands is a grim sight for Alliance explorers, given the northern nation's total silence behind the Greymane Wall."},kw={"amulet of grol","blasted lands","drowned sailor","gilneas","grol","shattershore","shipwreck"},rel={"zone:blastedlands","subzone:dark-portal","topic:alliance"},src={"Shattershore"}}
E["subzone:sunveil-excursion"] = {t="subzone",n="Sunveil Excursion",z="blastedlands",s="The Sunveil Excursion does not exist in the Blasted Lands of 25 ADP. The desolate southwestern reaches bordering the Tainted Scar remain untamed wasteland, untouched by sin'dorei archaeologists or organized research camps.",h="The Sunveil Excursion does not exist in the Blasted Lands of 25 ADP.",sec={{t="A Barren Frontier",b="Travelers wandering the southern rim of the Blasted Lands will find no trace of an encampment known as the Sunveil Excursion. In this era, the crimson wastes are defined by demonic intrusion, remnants of the Dark Portal's catastrophic legacy, and prowling beasts warped by fell energy. Organized archaeological expeditions into these foul margins have not occurred.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the Sunveil Excursion?",a="There is no Sunveil Excursion to be found in the Blasted Lands in 25 ADP. The area southwest near the Tainted Scar consists purely of scarred, lifeless wilderness populated by demons and beasts.",al={"sunveil excursion location","where is sunveil camp","find sunveil excursion"}},{q="Are there blood elf archaeologists here?",a="No. The blood elf research organization known as the Reliquary has established no presence in the southern Eastern Kingdoms at this time. The Horde's only foothold in the zone is Dreadmaul Hold further north.",al={"reliquary in blasted lands","blood elves in blasted lands","rohan sunveil"}},{q="What is currently located in this part of the Blasted Lands?",a="The southwestern sector lies immediately adjacent to the Tainted Scar, an infernal trench crawling with powerful demons and burning with fel magic left behind from the opening of the Dark Portal.",al={"what is southwest blasted lands","southwest blasted lands","tainted scar border"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Horde operatives traveling through the southern Blasted Lands must rely strictly on Dreadmaul Hold, as no forward expedition camps exist in the southwestern bluffs."},kw={"blasted lands","reliquary","rohan sunveil","sunveil","sunveil excursion","tainted scar"},rel={"zone:blastedlands","subzone:tainted-scar","subzone:dark-portal","topic:horde"},src={"Sunveil Excursion"}}
E["subzone:surwich"] = {t="subzone",n="Surwich",z="blastedlands",s="Surwich does not exist in this era. The jagged southwestern coast of the Blasted Lands remains a desolate, untamed shoreline battered by the sea and tainted by the fel energies spilling from the Dark Portal.",h="Surwich does not exist in this era.",sec={{t="A Wild and Desolate Shore",b="Travelers making their way along the southern precipices of the Blasted Lands will find no docks, cottages, or fishing nets. The region is a barren wasteland dominated by jagged red earth, prowling scavengers, and the shadow of the Dark Portal to the north. In 25 ADP, the only significant settlement in the entire region is Nethergarde Keep, built by the Alliance to watch the rift. Any quiet coastal haven here is purely a figment of a future that has not come to pass.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the town of Surwich?",a="Surwich does not exist in 25 ADP. The southwestern coast of the Blasted Lands where it would later be founded is currently unpopulated, rough wilderness.",al={"surwich location","find surwich","surwich map"}},{q="Are there any Gilnean settlements here?",a="No. The kingdom of Gilneas remains sealed entirely behind the colossal Greymane Wall in the north, isolated from the rest of the world and harboring no coastal colonies in the south.",al={"gilneans in blasted lands","gilneas refuge"}},{q="Where is the nearest flight path or outpost?",a="The sole Alliance stronghold in the Blasted Lands is Nethergarde Keep, situated to the north along the road out of the Swamp of Sorrows. To the west lies Stranglethorn Vale, where Booty Bay sits far down the southern cape.",al={"closest town","blasted lands flight path","where to rest"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Alliance explorers scouring the southern cliffs will find no friendly port or sanctuary beyond the fortified walls of Nethergarde Keep to the north."},kw={"blasted lands","coast","gilneas","nethergarde","surwich"},rel={"zone:blastedlands","subzone:nethergarde-keep","subzone:dark-portal","topic:alliance"},src={"Surwich"}}
E["subzone:tainted-scar"] = {t="subzone",n="Tainted Scar",z="blastedlands",s="The Tainted Scar is a demon-infested canyon carved into the southwestern Blasted Lands, saturated with foul fel magic from the nearby Dark Portal. It currently serves as the primary redoubt for the remnants of the Burning Legion on Azeroth, commanded by the doomguard Lord Kazzak.",h="The Tainted Scar is a demon-infested canyon carved into the southwestern Blasted Lands, saturated with foul...",sec={{t="A Bastion of the Legion",b="Once lush wetlands belonging to the ancient Black Morass, this desolate trench was utterly drained of life and turned the color of dried blood by chaotic fel energies leaking from the Dark Portal. Following Archimonde's defeat at Mount Hyjal during the Third War, surviving forces of the Burning Legion rallied in the south. The colossal ered'ruin Lord Kazzak claimed the Tainted Scar as his stronghold, stationing elite demons across its blackened rises and dispatching dreadful lieutenants like Razelikh the Defiler to hold dominion over the wasted red soils.",sp=0},{t="Unholy Inhabitants",b="While most mortals shun the Scar on pain of agonizing death, practitioners of the dark arts find its saturated fel energies irresistible. An eccentric human warlock named Daio the Decrepit has taken up residence by a ruined demonic altar overlooking the horrors, using the rampant fiends to perform dark rituals and instruct aspiring warlocks in how to summon and bind dread infernals.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Tainted Scar?",a="It is a canyon in the southwestern Blasted Lands heavily corrupted by demonic magic originating from the Dark Portal. Once part of the Black Morass, the land withered into a barren, blood-red wasteland populated almost entirely by high-ranking demons of the Burning Legion.",al={"what is tainted scar","tainted scar lore","why is the ground red here"}},{q="Who rules the Tainted Scar?",a="Lord Kazzak, a towering doomguard commander of the Burning Legion, oversees the demons gathered here. After the Legion's defeat in the Third War, he rallied the surviving fiends in the south to maintain a deadly foothold on Azeroth.",al={"who leads the demons here","tainted scar boss","lord kazzak tainted scar"}},{q="Why is an old human living among the demons here?",a="That hermit is Daio the Decrepit, an aged warlock who has braved the Scar to harness its potent fel ley energies. Rather than fleeing the demons, he conducts dark rituals at an altar here and mentors seasoned warlocks looking to master the summoning of infernals.",al={"who is daio","daio the decrepit","hermit in tainted scar"}},{q="Is the Tainted Scar connected to the Dark Portal?",a="Yes. When the Dark Portal first breached the boundary between worlds, chaotic Nether energies bled into the surrounding swamps. The Tainted Scar absorbed massive amounts of this magical fallout, permanently twisting the terrain into an inhospitable, demonic redoubt.",al={"tainted scar dark portal connection","why is it corrupted"}}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="The Tainted Scar is of great interest to veteran warlocks, who seek out Daio the Decrepit at his demonic altar to learn how to enslave and command fiery infernals.",["faction:Alliance"]="Alliance commanders closely monitor the canyon, fearful that Lord Kazzak's entrenched demon army could surge north into the Swamp of Sorrows or Stormwind territory."},kw={"blasted lands","burning legion","daio the decrepit","eredruin","kazzak","lord kazzak","razelikh","tainted scar"},rel={"zone:blastedlands","topic:burning-legion","npc:daio-the-decrepit","subzone:dark-portal","topic:third-war","topic:alliance","topic:horde"},src={"Tainted Scar"}}
E["zone:blastedlands"] = {t="zone",n="Blasted Lands",z="blastedlands",s="The Blasted Lands are a desolate expanse of red clay and barren rock at the southeastern tip of the Eastern Kingdoms, ruined by the chaotic energies of the Dark Portal. Once part of the verdant Black Morass, the shattered earth now harbors demonic remnants of the Burning Legion, brutal Dreadmaul ogres, and hardy desert beasts. Nethergarde Keep stands vigil over the desolate wasteland, guarding Azeroth from whatever horrors may spill out of the dormant gateway.",h="The Blasted Lands are a desolate expanse of red clay and barren rock at the southeastern tip of the Eastern...",sec={{t="A Scarred Wasteland",b="Before the First War, this region was a continuation of the dense fenlands known as the Black Morass. That lush swamp was utterly eradicated when the warlock Gul'dan and the possessed Medivh tore open the Dark Portal to unleash the orcish Horde. Chaotic fel energies bled through the dimensional breach, stripping all moisture and baking the earth into cracked red clay. When the portal frame was later destroyed at the end of the Second War, catastrophic shockwaves scorched the terrain further, transmuting the native stone into its unearthly crimson hue.",sp=0},{t="Nethergarde's Lonely Vigil",b="Perched upon the northern bluffs, Nethergarde Keep watches over the only road entering the valley. Commissioned by Archmage Khadgar and the Kirin Tor following the Second War, this stone bastion is manned by grim mages and stalwart soldiers sworn to prevent any renewed demonic or orcish incursions. It is an uninviting and strictly disciplined posting; infractions among the garrison are punished with banishment to the Stockade in Stormwind. The defenders face relentless pressure from the Dreadmaul ogres who stayed behind after Draenor's fall, raiding the roads and attacking the fortress gates under fell guidance.",sp=0},{t="The Legion's Remnant",b="In the southwestern reaches lies the Tainted Scar, a cratered canyon teeming with the deadliest demonic force on the continent. Stranded after the defeat at Mount Hyjal, the doomguard commander Lord Kazzak gathers wandering demons, doomguard, and felhounds to his banner. High above the red barrens, his dreadlord lieutenant, Razelikh the Defiler, orchestrates mortal servitude among the Shadowsworn cultists at the Altar of Storms and commands the local Dreadmaul ogres.",sp=0},{t="The Power of the Blood",b="Despite the land's desolation, scholars and wanderers brave its horrors for unique discoveries. Just inside the northern pass, Bloodmage Drazial and Bloodmage Lynnore conduct eccentric alchemical experiments, extracting organs from local scorpids, basilisks, and boars to brew extraordinarily potent physical enhancers. Farther into the wastes, a lone draenei hermit named Kum'isha seeks scattered draenethyst fragments, rewarding travelers who recover these alien remnants left behind by Draenor's shattered past.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is the ground red and barren?",a="The Blasted Lands were once part of the marshy Black Morass. When the Dark Portal opened, raw demonic magic drained the region of life and moisture. When Khadgar later destroyed the portal's stone framework with the Skull of Gul'dan, the resulting catastrophic explosion seared the clay into hard crimson earth.",al={"why is blasted lands red","why is it dead","what happened to the swamp"}},{q="What is the Dark Portal?",a="The Dark Portal is a massive dimensional gateway constructed to link Azeroth to Draenor, the sundered homeworld of the orcs now known as Outland. Though its stone frame was shattered to sever the bridge between worlds, the focal rift remains, guarded perpetually by Nethergarde Keep.",al={"where does dark portal go","is the portal open","what is the gateway"}},{q="Who controls Nethergarde Keep?",a="Nethergarde Keep is an Alliance bastion overseen by mages of the Kirin Tor and soldiers loyal to Stormwind. Built after the Second War under Archmage Khadgar's direction, its garrison maintains a strictly disciplined, dour watch over the Dark Portal and repels nearby ogre and demon attacks.",al={"who runs nethergarde","is nethergarde alliance","nethergarde mages"}},{q="What is the Tainted Scar?",a="The Tainted Scar is a demon-infested canyon in the southern Blasted Lands. It serves as a refuge for the remaining forces of the Burning Legion in the Eastern Kingdoms, spearheaded by the powerful doomguard Lord Kazzak and populated by doomguards, felguards, and felhounds.",al={"tainted scar elite area","who is in tainted scar","demon valley blasted lands"}},{q="Who are the blood elves camping near the entrance?",a="Bloodmage Drazial and Bloodmage Lynnore are researchers studying how the corrupted fauna adapted to the harsh fel landscape. In exchange for the entrails, brains, and lungs of native basilisks, vultures, scorpids, and boars, they brew powerful singular elixirs that bolster mortal attributes.",al={"blood elf buff potions","drazial and lynnore","boar lung quest"}},{q="Who is Kum'isha the Collector?",a="Kum'isha is an enigmatic draenei mystic dwelling in the central wastes. He collects draenethyst fragments and spheres—crystalline remnants originating from Draenor—and trades sealed packs of rare equipment and goods to anyone who brings them to him.",al={"draenei in blasted lands","kumisha","draenethyst quest"}},{q="How do you reach the Blasted Lands on foot?",a="Travel through Deadwind Pass east into the Swamp of Sorrows. From the Swamp of Sorrows, follow the primary road southward past the Horde settlement of Stonard until you reach the narrow mountain pass leading directly onto the red clay of the Blasted Lands.",al={"getting to blasted lands","how to get there","blasted lands entrance"}},{q="Why are there ogres living in the desert?",a="The Dreadmaul ogres crossed through the Dark Portal during the Second War. Rather than retreating back through the rift, they entrenched themselves within Dreadmaul Hold and fell under the thrall of the dreadlord Razelikh and the Shadowsworn cult.",al={"dreadmaul ogres lore","why are ogres here","dreadmaul hold"}}},ang={["class:Mage"]="The mages of Nethergarde Keep embody the stern, defensive application of the arcane, holding vigil against fel corruption and dimensional rifts left by Medivh's fall.",["class:Warlock"]="With the Tainted Scar swarming with high-ranking demons and Daio the Decrepit dwelling among the rocks, this desolate land offers seasoned warlocks unprecedented opportunities to bind dangerous fel entities.",["profession:Herbalism"]="The arid red clay is one of the extremely rare natural environments where Gromsblood grows, sprouted from ancient drops of demonic blood spilled upon the earth.",["faction:Alliance"]="Nethergarde Keep stands as your sole fortified haven in the region, guarding the southern reaches of the kingdom from horrors that could threaten Duskwood and Stormwind.",["faction:Horde"]="Though the Horde maintains no fortress here, the ruins of the Dark Portal serve as a grim monument to the Old Horde's crossing and the devastation wrought by demonic corruption."},kw={"black morass","blasted lands","dark portal","drazial","dreadmaul","gromsblood","kum'isha","lord kazzak","lynnore","nethergarde keep","razelikh","tainted scar"},rel={"subzone:dark-portal","subzone:nethergarde-keep","subzone:tainted-scar","zone:swampofsorrows","npc:bloodmage-drazial","npc:bloodmage-lynnore","npc:daio-the-decrepit","subzone:altar-of-storms-burning-steppes"},src={"Blasted Lands (Classic)","Blasted Lands"}}
